<title>ITALY: Rome April air cargo/mail traffic down 4.7pct.</title>
<headline>Rome April air cargo/mail traffic down 4.7pct.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rome airport operator said cargo and mail traffic at its Fuumincino Leonardo de Vinci and Ciampino airports, fell 4.7 percent to 21,678 tonnes against the same period 1996.</p>
<p>Cargo and mail handled by the two airports in tonnes with</p>
<p>the percentage change was as follows, official figure showed.</p>
<p>April 1997</p>
<p>		  Cargo    pct change     Mail	pct change</p>
<p>Fiumicino     20,867   down  5.9	3,391     up  9.5</p>
<p>Ciampino	   811     up 41.3	    0     n/a</p>
<p>Total	   21,678   down  4.7	3,391     up  9.5</p>
<p>Jan/Apr 97</p>
<p>		  Cargo    pct change     Mail	pct change</p>
<p>Fiumicino     76,594   down 11.7     14,114     up 10.0</p>
<p>Ciampino	 3,156     up 29.3	    0	  n/a</p>
<p>Total	   79,750   down 10.6	3,391     up 10.0</p>
<p>--Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542-7706 Fax+5017</p>
